<.shell current={:org_logo}>
  <h1>Org logo</h1>
  <p class="lead">A team's or organization's logo at 32px, or its initials when it has none.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <h2 class="heading media">
      <.org_logo id="org-logo-demo" src={~p"/images/sarduty-logo-square.svg"} name="SAR Duty" />
      SAR Duty site admins
    </h2>
    <h2 class="heading media">
      <.org_logo id="org-logo-demo-initials" name="Coastal SAR Association" />
      CSARA's organization admins
    </h2>
    <div class="media">
      <.org_logo id="org-logo-demo-name" name="Coast Range SAR" /> Coast Range SAR
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    Beside a team's or organization's name, or a heading about it, so people know whose it is at a glance: each section on Admins, and the organization on General.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    The team at the top of its Dashboard or General, which is 64px in the person head. A member, who gets their photo.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.org_logo id="…" src=&#123;url&#125; name=&#123;team.name&#125; /&gt;</code>
    shows the logo at <code>src</code>, or the first letters of the first two words of
    <code>name</code>
    when <code>src</code>
    is nil. Put it in a <code>.media</code>
    row, or a heading with <code>media</code>, so it sits beside the words.
  </p>
</.shell>
